      "summary": "The round-two tests now cover successful loader calls and exact view-model and descriptor mappings. However, the adapter trusts a caller-provided checksum instead of enforcing the checksum recorded for each authored asset.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "frontend/src/hangar/HangarCanvasAdapter.tsx",
          "line": 7,
          "message": "The caller-supplied provenance can replace the canonical checksum, so altered aircraft bytes can pass validation and reach the loader. This violates the required checksum-mismatch rejection and permits asset integrity bypass (OWASP A08:2025).",
          "confidence": 0.97,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The adapter checks the supplied provenance's path and category, then passes that record to loadValidatedHangarAsset. That validator verifies the bytes against the checksum in the supplied record; the adapter never compares that checksum with the canonical provenance record.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller supplies altered but structurally valid GLB bytes and a provenance record copied from the canonical record with its checksum and size updated to match. The adapter admits the bytes and calls the loader even though they do not match the authored asset's recorded checksum."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
